# Phase 5 transcript research: the Ctrl-O reading position across a page
# rebuild (026a8f4e, b1a53b01). Five reads make a document taller than the
# screen; then a command whose heading wraps to two rows while it is
# `Running` and fits one as `Ran`. Ctrl-O while it runs, a page up so the
# view stops following, then the same view after the command settles: its
# heading loses a row, a `* network:` record lands above the view, and the
# answer lands below. The first rows of the two snaps say whether it held.
gateway p5-transcript-anchor-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
work p5-transcript-ws
wait 4
type read and wait
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap running
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-running
key PPage
wait 1
snap full-pgup
key PPage
wait 1
snap full-pgup2
wait 10
snap full-pgup2-after
key C-o
wait 1
snap end
gwlog
